<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  DROIDWORKS_FULL_LIST_COEXIST_1. Every RSW_DW_ PawnKindDef using a humanlike
  (HAR) race needs initialResistanceRange/initialWillRange: vanilla's
  ConfigErrors() requires both on any humanlike-race PawnKindDef, since they
  back the vanilla recruit-by-resistance/will mechanic. None of the ~80
  JDS/KotOR/OuterRim droid kinds authored here set them, so a fresh full-list
  load (2026-09-08) logged one "initial resistance range is undefined" and one
  "initial will range is undefined" Config error per kind.

  Droids do not actually get talked down like a human prisoner; the values
  only need to exist to satisfy the engine. 10~20 / 5~10 matches the donor
  convention already used for humanlike droid kinds elsewhere in this mod's
  lineage (Outer Rim - Droid Depot's OuterRim_ImperialDTSeriesSentryDroid:
  initialResistanceRange 10~20, initialWillRange 5~10; see
  Source/extraction.json). PLACEHOLDER, not a balance pass: every kind gets
  the same flat range regardless of toughness. Revisit per-kind if resistance/
  will ever becomes load-bearing for droids specifically.
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[starts-with(defName, "RSW_DW_") and race and not(initialResistanceRange)]</xpath>
    <value>
      <initialResistanceRange>10~20</initialResistanceRange>
    </value>
  </Operation>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[starts-with(defName, "RSW_DW_") and race and not(initialWillRange)]</xpath>
    <value>
      <initialWillRange>5~10</initialWillRange>
    </value>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
